# Build context. Without this file, "docker build ." would send the daemon the
# whole directory, including a local .venv/ and the downloaded corpus, to build
# an image that only needs ingest/ and scripts/.
#
# Mind the distinction, which is the most confusing part: .dockerignore controls
# the CONTEXT (what the daemon can see), and COPY controls what goes into each
# layer. That is why tests/ and pyproject.toml are NOT excluded here: the
# runtime stage simply does not copy them, but the dev stage needs them.
#
# Unlike .gitignore, every pattern is matched from the root of the context: a
# bare "__pycache__/" only excludes ./__pycache__/, never ingest/__pycache__/.
# Anything that can appear at any depth needs the "**/" prefix.

# --- the most important one: a local virtual environment is built for the host
# (for example macOS arm64), is useless inside a Linux container, and would also
# shadow the container's environment.
.venv/
venv/

# Git history: no value at run time.
.git/
.gitignore

# Data. NONE of it goes into the image (see D-002):
#   data/raw/           4.8 MB of corpus, not versioned, mounted as a volume
#   data/processed/     2.1 MB of derived layer, regenerable
#   data/t2_nodes.json  1.8 MB, derived
#   data/manifest.json  mounted with the rest of data/, because the manifest and
#                       the corpus are a pair that must travel together. NOTE:
#                       nothing checks today that the manifest's sha256 is the
#                       hash of the RAW bytes. load_processed() only compares the
#                       processed layer's source_sha256 against the one DECLARED
#                       in the manifest, so a RAW file swapped behind its back
#                       would go unnoticed. Mounting them together is a
#                       convention, not a verified guarantee.
data/

# Tool caches and bytecode, at any depth. The bytecode is also built for another
# platform. Without "**/", the .pyc files in ingest/__pycache__/ reached the image.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Internal working documents: private and not versioned (see .gitignore). The
# fixture provenance note is the one Markdown file the dev stage keeps.
docs/
CLAUDE.md
**/*.md
!tests/fixtures/PROVENANCE.md

# Secrets: never in an image, at any depth.
**/.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key

# Local
**/.DS_Store
.claude/
